import streamlit as st
from PIL import Image


st.title("Need Finding Research")
st.subheader(
    "100 Ideas"
)
st.write("We were tasked with coming up with 100 ideas that our whitespace project could potentially be. To achieve this, our problem finding strategy consisted of personal and public observation as well as a questionnaire.")
st.write("Personal Observation:")
st.write("Over the course of the week, we took care to examine inconveniences in our own lives. Together we compiled our own personal grievances/observations to create problem statements.")
st.write("Questionnaire:")
st.write("We collaborated as a group to create an anonymous questionnaire. We tried to make the questions as unbiased and open ended as possible to allow for the interviewees to feel comfortable sharing any and all observations they have about their daily lives. Our target sample size was 30 people. We expected that we would get half of the responses back, which means that we sent out 60 forms. We contacted friends and family, as well as people in our classes chosen as random as possible. We also utilized social media platforms to reach a wider audience. We do not intend to follow up. ")
st.write("Our questionnaire followed this structure:")
st.write("  1. What kinds of pet peeves do you have?")
st.write("  2. Are there any tasks that you wish were easier or more convenient to do?")
st.write("  3. What's something that you had a problem doing in the past week?")
st.write("Public Observation")
st.write("To get a variety of problems, we observed people in a variety of different settings and noted what things they have difficulty with or tasks that seem to take a long time. Some places that we observed include Tech, the dining halls, dorm halls, and local stores (Whole Foods, Target, etc).")
st.write("Using the results:")
st.write("As a group we compiled the list of problems collected from the methods stated above and formalized each problem into a solvable statement. We got consent from all of our questionnaire responders to use their responses for our project. We did not conduct any interviews or collect any identifying information in our questionnaire.")
st.subheader("25 Ideas")
st.write("Our next task was to cut our list of 100 ideas down to 25. To do this, we first eliminated any duplicate survey responses and consolidated very similar ideas. For example, two ideas collected were to make backpacks more accessible while wearing them and to make backpacks more comfortable. We combined these two ideas into making easy-access comfortable backpacks. Afterwards, we eliminated any problems that were more policy-based in nature, rather than product-based. For example, changing the schedule of the Northwestern Loop shuttles would be more of a policy project and would be hard to create a product solution for. For the remaining ideas, we chose based on group interest. The 25 ideas we ended up with are listed thusly.")
st.image("25_ideas.png")
st.subheader("1 Idea")
st.write("To get down to our final idea, each group member chose one or two ideas that they were the most engaged with and did research on those ideas (Appendix B). Afterwards, based on the results of our research, we discussed with each other to find our final idea. We decided to go with the pool chalk problem.")
